\title{Inland-Buhi-Daraga Bikol Language Resources for K-12 Curriculum Development}
\author{Compiled by Claude Sonnet 5.5 (claude-sonnet-5-5) for Andr\'as Kornai}
\date{}
\begin{document}
\maketitle

\section{Introduction}
The code bhk (Inland-Buhi-Daraga Bikol, Glottolog alba1269) appears to be a retired ISO 639-3 code that was split into more specific codes; search results list it as deprecated. One successor variety, Buhi'non (ISO 639-3: ubl), is spoken around Buhi, Camarines Sur. No resources specific to ``Inland-Buhi-Daraga Bikol'' as a unit were found. The Buhi'non items below are listed as the closest related materials and should not be assumed to cover other Albay varieties.

\section{Primary Educational Resources}
\begin{itemize}
\item Buhi'non orthography booklet from the Komisyon sa Wikang Filipino, described as part of an effort to ease production of reading materials for mother-tongue-based multilingual education in Kindergarten to Grade 3: \url{https://kwfwikaatkultura.ph/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Boinen.pdf}
\end{itemize}

\section{Linguistic and Reference Materials}
\begin{itemize}
\item Glottolog entry for the Albay Bikol group: \url{https://glottolog.org/resource/languoid/id/alba1269.bigmap.html}
\item Wikipedia, Albay Bikol language: \url{https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Albay_Bikol_language}
\item Austronesian Basic Vocabulary Database, Bikol (Buhinon) word list: \url{https://abvd.eva.mpg.de/austronesian/language.php?id=710}
\item Bikol Grammar Notes (University of Hawai'i Press); based on standard Naga Bikol, so only indirectly applicable: \url{https://manifold.uhpress.hawaii.edu/projects/bikol-grammar-notes}
\end{itemize}

\section{Religious and Community Resources}
\begin{itemize}
\item Scripture Earth listing for Buhi'non (ubl), reported to include Gospel portions with audio: \url{https://scriptureearth.org/00eng.php?iso=ubl}
\end{itemize}

\section{Digital and Audio Resources}
\begin{itemize}
\item Global Recordings Network, Bikol, Buhi'non: \url{https://globalrecordings.net/en/language/ubl}
\end{itemize}

\section{Curriculum Development Context}
Albay-area varieties differ from town to town, and Buhi'non is spoken only in a small area around Lake Buhi. Standard Bikol materials from Naga may not suit these speakers well. Before curriculum work, the intended variety and its current ISO code should be settled with local educators.

\end{document}
